WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:06.707
Swallow flew slowly back to the statue.

2
00:00:06.708 --> 00:00:10.457
"Swallow, what are you doing here?

3
00:00:10.458 --> 00:00:14.457
Did you find the children under the bridge?"

4
00:00:14.458 --> 00:00:23.166
Swallow sighed. "Yes. They were happy to receive the jewel."

5
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:28.582
"So why do [i@you@i] look sad?" the statue asked.

6
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:33.749
"There are many other people who need help," Swallow said.

7
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.582
"I can't think only of myself and leave for Egypt."

8
00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:43.041
"Then let's help more people," the statue said.

9
00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:50.582
"How?" Swallow asked. "You have no more jewels."

10
00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:57.874
"I have something else," the statue said. "Gold!"

11
00:00:57.875 --> 00:01:00.999
Swallow stared at him.

12
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.874
"But if I remove your gold, Prince, you will be bare.

13
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:09.666
And the townspeople will be angry."

14
00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:13.582
"Then let them be angry," the statue said.

15
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:17.666
"I care more about the people who need help."

16
00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.764
Swallow flapped his wings.

17
00:01:20.765 --> 00:01:24.416
"Your kindness inspires me!"

18
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:28.541
And so, he got to work.

19
00:01:28.542 --> 00:01:33.749
Slowly he peeled some gold off the back of the statue's head.

20
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.691
Swallow took that gold and flew to a small house.

21
00:01:38.692 --> 00:01:44.416
A mother and her four children were sharing one potato.

22
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:48.577
Swallow dropped the gold at the mother's feet.

23
00:01:48.578 --> 00:01:51.746
Then he flew off to get more gold.

24
00:01:51.747 --> 00:01:55.707
He could make someone else happy!

25
00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:59.538
Swallow spent the rest of the day that way.

26
00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:03.041
He pulled off pieces of gold.

27
00:02:03.042 --> 00:02:09.624
Then he delivered them to people in need.

28
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:13.486
"Now we have money!" a man said.

29
00:02:13.487 --> 00:02:24.249
His wife cheered. "Oh! Hooray! We can buy food and fix our home!"

30
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.353
"Phew! I'm tired," Swallow thought.

31
00:02:28.354 --> 00:02:34.291
"But the people's joy keeps me going."

32
00:02:34.292 --> 00:02:38.832
Again he returned to the statue to gather more gold.

33
00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:42.926
By now a crowd was gathered there.

34
00:02:42.927 --> 00:02:48.533
"Our statue is turning dull and gray!" someone shouted.

35
00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:55.291
"Somebody is stealing all its gold—and its beauty!"

36
00:02:55.292 --> 00:02:59.290
"We must catch the thief!"

37
00:02:59.291 --> 00:03:08.624
Swallow gulped. "If they see me, they might try to kill me!" he thought.

38
00:03:08.625 --> 00:03:12.235
He flew toward a tree near the statue.

39
00:03:12.236 --> 00:03:17.079
He was about to land when he spotted the hawk perched there.

40
00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:21.916
It glared at him.

41
00:03:21.917 --> 00:03:27.207
Swallow shot back to the statue.

42
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:33.749
"What's wrong?" the statue asked. "You look scared."

43
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:38.707
"I think that hungry hawk is following me!"

44
00:03:38.708 --> 00:03:46.832
"You must fly away!" the statue said. "Go, hurry!"

45
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:52.048
Swallow shook his head. "There are still people in need.

46
00:03:52.049 --> 00:03:58.582
I will leave after we help more of them."

47
00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:02.891
That night Swallow lay at the statue's feet.

48
00:04:02.892 --> 00:04:09.374
But with all the gold gone, the statue felt hard and cold.

49
00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:17.883
Swallow curled up tightly and tried not to shiver.

